# Install as /etc/seg-demo/visual-hub.env with mode 0600.
# Never commit real credentials.
#
# These are FACTORY DEFAULTS, not hard requirements. Every role can be rebound
# from the Visual Hub UI, which persists the choice in
# configs/_camera_bindings.yaml (see the "Choose a camera per module" section of
# the README). A role left blank simply refuses to start until a camera is
# picked; the hub itself boots with no environment file at all.
FRONT_CAMERA_URL=rtsp://USER:PASSWORD@FRONT_CAMERA_IP:554/
REAR_CAMERA_URL=rtsp://USER:PASSWORD@REAR_CAMERA_IP:554/
# Cabin default. It is no longer frozen to usb:0 — any detected source
# (usb:<idx> | rtsp://... | video:<file> | image:<path> | synthetic) is allowed,
# but a bare USB index is what the role is calibrated and sized for.
DMS_CAMERA=usb:0
HUB_PORT=8000
SEG_DEMO_RUNTIME_OVERRIDES=/home/seeed/workspace/seg_demo/configs/_runtime_overrides.yaml
# Optional: spare PoE cameras offered in the picker without first promoting them
# to FRONT/REAR_CAMERA_URL. Comma separated, credentials allowed.
# HUB_EXTRA_CAMERAS=rtsp://USER:PASSWORD@SPARE_CAMERA_IP:554/
# Optional: where the UI writes the per-role bindings (default: repo-local
# configs/_camera_bindings.yaml). Point this at a writable, non-versioned path
# when the checkout is read-only for the service user.
# HUB_CAMERA_BINDINGS=/var/lib/seg-demo/camera_bindings.yaml
# Optional: keep recordings on a larger mounted disk when available.
VISUAL_HUB_RECORDING_ROOT=/home/seeed/Videos/visual-hub